The GBM devices and the shared display outlive the exit handlers.

DRMDeviceManager::singleton() was a function-local std::unique_ptr, so its
destructor ran from the exit handlers -- and it owns the GBM devices, each of
which owns the driver screen that every EGL display and GL context on it
renders through.  A web process ending while one of Skia's GPU painting
threads was still tearing down its thread_local GL context crashed in the
driver: the main thread had freed the screen (gbm_device_destroy) and the
worker's glDeleteProgram read the freed buffer manager (SIGSEGV at 0x229 in
vmw_dma_buffer_unmap).  Both singletons are now never destroyed; the shared
display's EGL display is still terminated by its own exit handler.

